pack compute-governance-closed
generation control-1
provenance closing the three gaps called out 2026-08-27 -- Claude unmetered, commons coverage incomplete, spend governed by an env var
authority measured
note Continues compute-financial-metabolism. Three demands, three closures, and the largest single finding in the session: actual compute spend is roughly nineteen times the declared budget, and nothing was watching.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. CLAUDE METERED -- and it is the whole bill
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

upgrade upg:claude-in-the-ledger
  status LANDED
  verification MEASURED
  claim Claude usage is now metered into the same financial membrane as OpenAI.
  receipts 241 Claude Code session transcripts under ~/.claude/projects, 22,253 assistant messages carrying a usage block per message
  scale claude-sonnet-5 5,290,720,872 cache reads; claude-opus-5 1,739,687,925; claude-opus-4-8 1,606,416,885
  totals fresh input 88,521; cache writes 93,464,252; cache reads 8,636,825,682; output 19,633,885
  priced $5,748.75 at published rates, against OpenAI's $18.85 -- Claude is 99.7% of measured compute spend
  basis billed, via rung 2 (published book by exact model id)
  caveat claude-opus-4-8 resolved to anthropic/claude-opus-4 by family match, so that line is approximate

claim clm:anthropic-admin-key-is-not-an-admin-key
  status STANDING
  verification REPRODUCED
  claim The ANTHROPIC_AI_ADMIN_API_KEY added to provider.refs.env cannot reach org endpoints.
  evidence prefix is sk-ant-api03-, which is a standard API key; Anthropic Admin keys are sk-ant-admin01-
  evidence /v1/organizations/cost_report, /usage_report/messages, /workspaces, /api_keys and /users all return 403 permission_error
  consequence Claude stays at cascade rung 2 (published book) rather than rung 1 (derived from billing), so its $5,748.75 is list-rate and cannot reflect contract terms
  action_required an Admin key minted by an org Owner under Console -> Admin keys would promote Claude to rung 1, the same way OPEN_AI_ADMIN_API_KEY did for OpenAI
  note the cascade degraded correctly and labelled the basis it earned rather than guessing

claim clm:cache-is-87-percent-of-avoided-cost
  status STANDING
  verification MEASURED
  claim Prompt caching is doing almost all of the token-cost work, and its value is now quantified on both providers.
  anthropic read:write ratio 92.4:1; caching avoided $38,890.29 of an otherwise $44,519.50 bill -- 87% avoided
  openai 58.2% of input served cached; caching avoided $7.4721 of an otherwise $26.85 bill -- 39% avoided
  asymmetry Anthropic cache WRITES cost more than fresh input while READS cost far less, so the workload is only cache-positive because reads outnumber writes 92:1; that ratio is measured here, not assumed
  consequence cache hit rate is the highest-leverage token lever in the estate, and it is now a billed quantity rather than a belief

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. COMMONS COVERAGE CLOSED COMPLETELY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

upgrade upg:coverage-closed
  status LANDED
  verification MEASURED
  before 112 profiles; 49% of the map's own hook answer key unreachable
  after 176 profiles, 6 aliases, 0 unauthored specialties, 0% of the answer key unreachable
  method 65 names already present; 66 new profiles created with authored specialty; 6 recorded as aliases against existing partner_ids so no duplicate identity was created
  authored specialty text for the 66 is authored here rather than extracted, and every observation records which, so a later reader can tell knowledge from transcription
  proof the token-reduction query that previously failed now answers correctly

claim clm:token-query-now-answerable
  status STANDING
  verification MEASURED
  before latent query for token reduction returned Weights & Biases, DVC, JSON Schema, ArcticDB, MLflow -- lifecycle and billing profiles, because every real method was missing
  after returns caveman, llama.cpp/GGUF, GigaToken, BitNet, rtk, ggml -- output compression, local inference, context coordinates, ternary quantization, CLI output filtering, tensor kernels
  consequence the commons can now answer the question it exists to answer; the coverage gap was not cosmetic

defect def:substring-aliasing-corrupts-identity
  status FIXED
  verification REPRODUCED
  claim Loose substring matching produced four wrong partner identities before it was caught.
  wrong quickfix -> QUIC (a FIX session protocol engine mapped onto a transport protocol)
  wrong oracle_oci -> OCI (Oracle Cloud Infrastructure mapped onto Open Container Initiative)
  wrong DSSE/SARIF/VEX/OpenTelemetry -> Tel
  wrong github_discovery -> Git
  fix a name with authored specialty is a DISTINCT method and is never aliased; otherwise suffix-stripped equality only
  note this is the third time in this session that substring matching silently corrupted a result set; the earlier two were "Git" swallowing "GitHub discovery" in the hook answer key, and the same pattern in name resolution. Substring matching on identity is not safe anywhere in this estate.

